<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marcus Petreius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 110–46 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marcus Petreius was a Roman soldier who commanded the army that defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catiline">Catiline</a> at Pistoria in 62 BCE. A loyal legate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>, he fought against Caesar in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 49 BCE and then in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. After the defeat at Thapsus in 46 BCE he and King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juba-i">Juba I of Numidia</a>, refused shelter by Zama, died in a suicide pact by fighting each other.</p></div>
